# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession gathering build` from data/forever and tools/lib/professions/gathering. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/fishing-cooking
title Fishing + Cooking 1-300
category Professions
coords era
levels 5-60
zone Ironforge

# Fishing and Cooking 1-300 together, for both factions: each fishing band
# catches the fish its cooking takes, so neither waits on the other. Each band
# fishes a round of stands: the places players stood when they caught the
# band's fish there (Polestar_Recorder sessions, three or more players each), in
# a loop the arrow walks, leaving out stands near creatures more than a level
# above the band's level and near the other faction's towns. Starting areas to
# 75 (Cooking 50), the capitals to 150 (Cooking 140: city water beside the
# cooking trainer), catfish water to 190 (Cooking 175), Mithril Head Trout
# water to 225, Nat Pagle and Clamlette Surprise for Artisan, Tanaris to 300.
#
# What bites at a round: the recorded catches at its stands (150 or more), else
# the zone's fishing loot from Forever's server data; when a water loses no fish:
# its base fishing skill + 95 (Forever's server data). Recipes, their skill
# colours, prices and sellers are the data's (professions.json, Cooking).
# ASSUMED: catches per point follow Classic's rate (every catch below 75, then
# one in (skill - 50) / 25), cooking skill-ups the Classic chance; the fish a
# band holds you for are the expected crafts' worth.
# Not routed: the Ravaged Fishing Pole (one source, no loot row in the server
# data), Recipe: Plated Armorfish (one source), the Winter Frontier Fishery
# quests (Winter Squid only bites in winter).
#
# Spawns come from the reference data: the Era baseline (pfQuest) plus the
# node spawns Forever's beta sniffs add (Zephras Isle, the starting-area Poor
# Copper Veins and herbs: the Forever TrinityCore world DB); trainer learn skills
# and prices from Forever's sniffed trainer lists; recipes and their skill colours
# from the Forever client tables (`forge data professions`).
# ASSUMED: past level 30 (the beta's cap) Forever's spawns are Classic's; nothing
# confirms them yet. In-game check: refine with Polestar_Recorder sessions.
# Rank level gates: Journeyman Fishing asks level 10 (Forever's sniffed trainer
# list); Cooking's and First Aid's Journeyman ask none (their sniffed lists, and
# players' recordings train them at 6 and 7). In-game check: reading an Expert
# book below level 20.
# Waypoints are Era-frame (`coords era`); the engine converts them where Forever
# changed a map frame, and a map without an Era frame (Zephras Isle) compiles live.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice

step Learn Fishing and Cooking
  tip Any Fishing trainer of your faction teaches Apprentice Fishing (1s) and any Cooking trainer Apprentice Cooking (1s), at any character level; the arrow picks the nearest of each, and every starting area has both. Buy a Fishing Pole (23c) and equip it (you can only fish with a pole in your hands). Forever: every cook knows Basic Campfire: a Basic Campfire Kit from one Simple Wood with Flint and Tinder lights a cooking fire anywhere, so you can cook beside the water. If you sat at your starting area's campfire for The Great Outdoors, its camping guide also offers Camping 101: Fishing (handed in at Fishing 20 for the Fish Bowl recipe) and Camping 101: Cooking.
  train Fishing Apprentice
  train Cooking Apprentice
  buy 6256 x1 nearest

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Fishing 1-75

step Recipes for Elwynn Forest (Cooking to 50)
  only Human
  when !skill Cooking 50
  zone Elwynn Forest
  tip Before the round: Recipe: Brilliant Smallfish (Cooking 1, 40c: Tharynn Bouden, Elwynn Forest). A recipe teaches itself when you use it from your bags.
  buy 6325 x1 npc 66

step Lures for Elwynn Forest
  only Human
  when !skill Fishing 25
  tip This water loses fish below Fishing 25: a lure on the pole adds to your skill for ten minutes. Shiny Bauble (+25, 50c each) closes the gap from 1; three see you through.
  buy 6529 x3 nearest

step Fishing: Elwynn Forest (1-75)
  only Human
  when !skill Cooking 50
  zone Elwynn Forest
  tip Fish the round until Fishing 75 and until your bags hold 50 Raw Brilliant Smallfish for the cooking: about 80 catches (below 75 every catch raises the skill). The arrow leads stand to stand: stay while you catch fish (casting holds the arrow there), walk on when a pool is fished out or the spot is busy. What bites here (players' catches at these stands): Raw Brilliant Smallfish (61%), Raw Longjaw Mud Snapper (37%). This water loses fish below skill 25: keep a lure on the pole until then.
  loop
  goto 47.1,64.0 r 15
  goto 48.8,63.3 r 15
  goto 47.5,63.3 r 15
  goto 39.7,65.6 r 15
  goto 46.6,64.7 r 15
  collect 6291 x50 anywhere
  skill Fishing 75

step Fishing: Elwynn Forest (1-75)
  only Human
  when skill Cooking 50
  zone Elwynn Forest
  tip Your Cooking is past 50, so there are no fish to keep: fish the round until Fishing 75, about 70 catches.
  loop
  goto 47.1,64.0 r 15
  goto 48.8,63.3 r 15
  goto 47.5,63.3 r 15
  goto 39.7,65.6 r 15
  goto 46.6,64.7 r 15
  skill Fishing 75

step Cook Brilliant Smallfish (1-50)
  only Human
  tip Brilliant Smallfish is orange from 1 (yellow at 45, green at 65, grey at 85): about 50 crafts to 50, 50 Raw Brilliant Smallfish. Cook at any fire: a town hearth or your own Basic Campfire. Short of fish: fish the round a little longer.
  learn 7751
  craft 7751 until 50

step Journeyman Cooking
  only Human
  tip Journeyman Cooking raises the cap to 150; it needs skill 50 and no character level, and costs 5s. The arrow picks the nearest Cooking trainer of your faction.
  train Cooking Journeyman

